{
  "entity0": {
    "rationale": "Evidence from iteration 2 (the best so far, 713.6): the oval finishes 20/20 (rms 0.006 m, 0 line losses), and the s-bend finishes 19/20 (one off-track). The slalom is the failure: 0/20 finishes, progress 0.63, about 1.05 line-loss events per run, and every run ends off track. Its steering oscillation (0.31) and rms (0.017 m) are similar to the s-bend, so the main problem is that the 5-sensor array spans only ±2 cm and loses the tape when the robot drifts or the line swings sideways on sharp bends. Change: widen the sensor spread to ±3 cm (x = -0.03, -0.015, 0, 0.015, 0.03), so the outer sensors still see tape at larger offsets and sum(readings) falls below 0.05 less often. To keep the loop gain unchanged, the sensor weights are scaled by 1.5 (-3, -1.5, 0, 1.5, 3), which makes the signal about 1.5 times larger for the same offset. kp is therefore divided by 1.5 (1.5 to 1.0), and kd is scaled to 0.4 (0.6 divided by 1.5), so the wheel-command response per cm of error is about the same as before. base_speed (1.2), mass (0.6), body, wheel_track (0.14), wheel_radius, sensor size (0.016), sensor y (0.05), ki (0) and line_loss (last_direction) are kept, so the spread change is the only variable that moves. Expected result: slalom line_loss_events fall below 0.5 and slalom progress rises above 0.8, with the first slalom finishes possible; the oval stays at finish rate 1.0 and the s-bend holds near 0.95. Hypotheses: (H1) the wider spread cuts line losses on the slalom by more than half; (H2) the rescaled gain keeps steering_oscillation near 0.3 or below; (H3) the wider sensor array does not raise noise sensitivity on the oval. Measurements wanted: completion, progress, completion_time, rms_error, max_error, line_loss_events, steering_oscillation, control_effort and noise_robustness per track, so I can check whether the slalom losses drop and whether the gain rescale holds the oval and s-bend.",
    "geometry": {
      "body_length": 0.14,
      "body_width": 0.12,
      "mass": 0.6,
      "sensor_positions": [
        {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.05}
      ],
      "sensor_size": 0.016,
      "wheel_radius": 0.03,
      "wheel_track": 0.14
    },
    "controller": {
      "base_speed": 1.2,
      "kp": 1.0,
      "ki": 0.0,
